{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_cockroachdb", "label": "CockroachDB", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Laeuft auf den unveraenderten Postgres-Stores - es gibt kein CockroachJournal. Zertifiziert durch test:integration:cockroachdb.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_yugabytedb", "label": "YugabyteDB (YSQL)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Liefert YSQL auf Port 5433 statt 5432 und formuliert bekanntermassen einige Postgres-Fehlermeldungen um. Zertifiziert durch test:integration:yugabytedb; initialisiert beim ersten Start seine System-Kataloge und braucht merklich laenger als jedes andere Image der Matrix.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_wire_compatibility", "label": "PostgreSQL-Wire-Kompatibilitaet", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Wire-Kompatibilitaet gibt das Protokoll, nicht automatisch identische Semantik - deshalb wird sie getestet statt angenommen. Beide Suiten fahren denselben Contract wie die Postgres-Suite, sodass ein kuenftiges Auseinanderlaufen Upstream einen CI-Job rot faerbt statt in Produktion aufzutauchen. Zertifiziert ist nur die zertifizierte Oberflaeche: nicht der Tag-Pfad von PersistenceQuery und nichts ausserhalb von Persistence; Neon, Timescale, AlloyDB und Aurora funktionieren sehr wahrscheinlich, stehen aber genau deshalb nicht in der Tabelle.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_sqlstate_matching", "label": "Fehlerklassifikation ueber SQLSTATE statt Meldungstext", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Der Backstop matcht auf SQLSTATE, nie auf Meldungstext - wichtig, weil YugabyteDB Postgres-Fehlermeldungen umformuliert (yugabyte-db#9294). Eine textbasierte Implementierung waere still gescheitert, und zwar auf die schlechteste denkbare Weise: ein echter Konflikt kaeme als generischer Fehler an.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_serializable_40001", "label": "SERIALIZABLE-Abbruch 40001 statt 23505", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Beide Engines fahren auf SERIALIZABLE und brechen die verlierende Transaktion ab, bevor sie den Primary Key erreicht - sie melden 40001, wo PostgreSQL 23505 meldet. Ein Contention-Abort beweist aber nur, dass die Engine ein Opfer gewaehlt hat, nicht dass jemand anderes geschrieben hat: die Stores lesen den Head neu und melden nur einen Konflikt, wenn er sich wirklich bewegt hat, sonst liefe der Caller in eine Retry-Schleife gegen einen Head, der sich nie aendert.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_distributed_write_latency", "label": "Verteilte Write-Latenz", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Beide Datenbanken replizieren synchron per Konsens, ein Journal-Append kostet also einen Raft-Round-Trip statt eines lokalen fsync. Aggressiver snapshotten als bei Single-Node-Postgres und das Actor-System in derselben Region halten.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_cockroachdb", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_postgres_postgresjournal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_yugabytedb", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_postgres_postgresjournal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_wire_compatibility", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_postgres_postgresjournal", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_sqlstate_matching", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_postgres_concurrency_backstop", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_sqlstate_matching", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_yugabytedb", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_serializable_40001", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_postgres_concurrency_backstop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_serializable_40001", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_mariadb_contention_backstop", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_distributed_write_latency", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_wire_compatibility", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_cockroachdb", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_yugabytedb", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_wire_compatible_wire_compatibility", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_cloudflare_d1_verification_gap", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/wire-compatible.mdx", "source_location": null,